    {
      "title": "Messi scores and assists as Inter Miami play out 2-2 draw against Union",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/sports/football-news/messi-scores-and-assists-as-inter-miami-play-out-2-2-draw-against-union-126082000146_1.html",
      "description": "Lionel Messi had a goal and assist as Inter Miami and the Philadelphia Union played to a 2-2 draw.\nMessi's cross was headed by Luis Suarez into the path of forward Daniel Pinter for the first Inter Miami goal in the 21st minute Wednesday night.\nMessi cut inside to his preferred left foot from 12 yards out in the 26th and curled a shot into the corner of the net for his first goal since returning to action following the death of his father.\nMessi has 13 goals and nine assists in 17 MLS games this season. He has six goals and four assists in six matches in all competitions against the Union.\nIndiana Vassilev scored on a volley in the first half to give the Union the lead, then 18-year-old defender Neil Pierre headed home his third goal in five games this season in the 58th minute to tie the score. Cavan Sullivan, the Union's 16-year-old midfielder, was credited with his seventh assist of the season on Vassilev's goal.\nUnion forward Milan Iloski appeared to put the Union ahead in the",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-20T08:18:23"
    }
  ]
